      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\n**Code Simplicity \u0026 Idiomaticity**: Passing a struct with a flexible array member by C++ reference (`const struct ec_response_fp_info_v3 \u0026info`) invokes undefined behavior when accessing the array elements (`info.image_frame_params[i]`), as the compiler may assume the reference spans only `sizeof(ec_response_fp_info_v3)` bytes. \n\nYou can eliminate this UB and significantly simplify the test code by decoupling `populate_from_info` from the `ec_response_fp_info_v3` wrapper struct. If you pass the params array and `num_types` directly, the test cases no longer need the dummy `struct { info; params[N]; } packet` wrappers.\n\n```cpp\nvoid FpImageFrameParamsCache::populate_from_info(\n\tconst struct fp_image_frame_params_v2 *params,\n\tuint8_t num_types,\n\tuint32_t max_image_buffer_bytes)\n{\n\tframe_params_.fill({});\n\n\tif (num_types \u003e frame_params_.size()) {\n\t\tCPRINTS(\"ERROR - EC returned %u types, max supported is %zu.\",\n\t\t\tnum_types, frame_params_.size());\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\n\tstd::array\u003cFpImageFrameParam, FP_CAPTURE_TYPE_MAX\u003e new_params{};\n\tfor (uint8_t i \u003d 0; i \u003c num_types; ++i) {\n\t\tconst auto \u0026raw \u003d params[i];\n\n\t\tif (!validate(raw, max_image_buffer_bytes)) {\n\t\t\treturn;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tnew_params[raw.fp_capture_type] \u003d {\n\t\t\t.frame_size_bytes \u003d raw.frame_size,\n\t\t\t.image_data_offset_bytes \u003d raw.image_data_offset_bytes,\n\t\t};\n\t}\n\n\tframe_params_ \u003d new_params;\n}\n```\n\nThen `populate_cache` can just call:\n```cpp\n\tpopulate_from_info(info-\u003eimage_frame_params, info-\u003esensor_info.num_capture_types, max_image_buffer_bytes);\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/cns/gg-d/home/tomhughes@google.com/review_trajectories/cl8499506_108095cf-d069-4cd8-be24-23fb65d5ccb6.pb)",
